{
  "message": "With 40–60 hours available, a rough jump and one short level fit this checkpoint. Starting without tasks or a shown build is common and fixable within these four weeks. Before approving, add the three steps below so we can check progress against something playable. I’ll check in after the first sprint and look forward to your build and devlog ;).",
  "tasks": [],
  "add": [
    "Week 1: Make movement and jumping playable in a plain test room, including landing and restarting after a fall, and share an openable build.",
    "Week 2: Build one short level around the jump, with a clear start, finish and restart, and share an openable build.",
    "Weeks 3–4: Ask two people to open and play the level without help, fix problems that prevent completion, and publish a short devlog with findings and the updated build link."
  ],
  "goal": {
    "fit": "fits",
    "note": "The goal fits 40–60 hours if the first level stays short and uses placeholder art. Treat “anyone can open” as something outside players must test, not just a build you can run yourself.",
    "stage": {
      "inside": true,
      "note": ""
    }
  }
}

